KNOWN GAP, owned by `a-composed-recipe-segment-arrives-without-its-lines`.

A recipe cut into segments around a composed `$(MAKE)` reaches the graph as an
assembled script per segment: kati hands `SinkSubninja::preceding` and
`residual_command` over as text and withholds the per-line steps, so nothing
downstream knows which of those lines carried the `+`. One launch has one
answer to "does this run anyway", and it is no — marking the whole script would
have `-t` run every line of it, which is the mode breaking its own promise.

GNU Make 4.4.1 runs both marked lines and touches `goal`. Ronin touches `goal`
and runs neither. Decided on `pretending-over-an-assembled-recipe`.
